NATIONAL ASSEM BLY SECRETARIAT
4. MR, AHAD KHAN CHEEMA, Minister for Establishment, to introduce a Bill further to amendthe National School of Public Policy Ordinance, 2002 ffhe National School of Public Policy(Amendment) 8ill, 20251.
5. MR. QAISER AHMED SHEIKH, Minister for Board of lnvestment, to introduce a Bill to providefor reforms of the regulatory regime applicable to business, trade and investment by removingcumbersome and complex regulatory requirements and to establish the Pakistan Regulatory Registryand the Pakistan Business Portal [The Asaan Karobar Bill, 2025].
PRESENTATION OF REPORTS OF THE STANDING COMMITTEES
5. CH. MAHMOOD BASHIR VIRK, Chairman Standing Committee on Law and Justice, to movethat the delay in the presentation of the report of the Standing Committee on the Bill further toamend the National Accountability Ordinance, 1999 [The National Accountability (Amendment) Bill,2024),ltl today be condoned.
7. CH. MAHMOOD BASHIR VIRK, Chairman Standing Committee on Law and Justice, to presentthe report of the Standing Committee on the Bill further to amend the National AccountabilityOrdinance, 1999 [The National Accountability (Amendment) 9il,2024).
8. CH. MAHMOOD BASHIR VIRK, Chairman Standing Committee on Law and Justice, to movethat the delay in the presentation of the report of the Standing Committee on the Bill further toamend the Civil Servants Act, 1973 [The Civil Servants (Amendment) Bill, 2025], till today becondoned.
9. CH. MAHMOOD BASHIR VIRK, Chairman Standing Committee on Law and Justice, to presentthe report of the Standing Committee on the Bill further to amend the Civil Servants Act, 1973 [TheCivil Serva nts (Amendment) Bill,2025l.
10. MR. TATEH ULLAH KHAN, Chairman Standing Committee on Defence, to move that the delayin the presentation of the report of the Standing Committee on the Bill further to amend the PakistanNavy Ordinance, 1961 [The Pakistan Navy (Amendment) Bill, 2025], till today be condoned.
11. MR. FATEH UTLAH KHAN, Chairman Standing Committee on Defence, to present the report ofthe Standing Committee on the Billfurther to amend the Pakistan Navy Ordinance, 1961 [The PakistanNavy (Amendment) Bill, 20251.
ORDERS OF THE DAYfor the meeting of the National Assembly to be held on Monday, the 5th May, 2025 at 5.OO p.m.L. Tilowat. Hodith, Noot and national anthem.QUESTIONS2. Questions entered in a separate list to be asked and answers given.CATLING ATTENTION NOTICE3. MS. SEHAR KAMRAN to invite attention of the Minister for Finance and Revenue, to a matterof urgent public importance regarding imposition of 18% sales tax on cotton, causing grave concernamongst the pu blic.INTRODUCTION OF BITLS

